# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">05</span><span class="sec-icon">📄</span><h2>CSV and the rescued data column</h2></div><p>CSV needs options. The defaults often give a single column, or headers loaded as data:</p>
# MAGIC <div class="code"><div class="code-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="lang">SQL</span><button class="copy" type="button">copy</button></div><pre><span style="color: #FF7B72">SELECT</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">*</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">FROM</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">read_files(</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">'/Volumes/shop/raw/sales-csv/'</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">,</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">format</span><span style="color: #6E7681">    </span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">=&gt;</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">'csv'</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">,</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">header</span><span style="color: #6E7681">    </span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">=&gt;</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">true</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">,</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">delimiter</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">=&gt;</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">'|'</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">,</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #FF7B72">schema</span><span style="color: #6E7681">    </span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">=&gt;</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">'order_id INT, email STRING, amount DOUBLE'</span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">,</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #6E7681">  </span><span style="color: #E6EDF3">rescuedDataColumn</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #FF7B72; font-weight: bold">=&gt;</span><span style="color: #6E7681"> </span><span style="color: #A5D6FF">'_rescued_data'</span>
# MAGIC <span style="color: #E6EDF3">);</span></pre></div>
# MAGIC <ul>
# MAGIC <li><strong><code>_rescued_data</code></strong> catches values that don't match the schema (wrong type, extra columns) as JSON, so <strong>nothing is silently lost</strong>.</li>
# MAGIC <li>When the schema is inferred, <code>read_files</code> / Auto Loader add <code>_rescued_data</code> automatically.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Missing header? Set <code>header =&gt; false</code> and supply the column names through <code>schema</code>.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Typical lab pattern: ingest, inspect rows <code>WHERE _rescued_data IS NOT NULL</code>, then fix and coalesce them.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

