# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">07</span><span class="sec-icon">🔀</span><h2>Enterprise sources: Lakeflow Connect managed connectors</h2></div><ul>
# MAGIC <li>In the workspace, open <strong>Data Ingestion</strong>. It shows the Databricks connectors, file upload, and Fivetran (partner) connectors.</li>
# MAGIC <li>A managed connector creates an <strong>ingestion pipeline</strong>:</li>
# MAGIC <li>a <strong>connection</strong> (credentials stored as a UC object);</li>
# MAGIC <li>the source objects to sync;</li>
# MAGIC <li>the destination <strong>catalog and schema</strong>.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>SaaS connectors</strong> run fully serverless. <strong>Database connectors</strong> add an <strong>ingestion gateway</strong> that reads the change log (CDC).</li>
# MAGIC <li>Each source table lands as a <strong>streaming table</strong>, with history as <strong>SCD Type 1</strong> (overwrite) or <strong>SCD Type 2</strong> (keep history).</li>
# MAGIC <li>Schedule it from the pipeline itself or from a Lakeflow Job.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC <blockquote class="callout">
# MAGIC <p>Federation <strong>queries data in place</strong>. Lakeflow Connect <strong>ingests</strong> it. These are different tools for different needs.</p>
# MAGIC </blockquote>
# MAGIC </div>

